| Hotel | Why you might like it |
|-------|----------------------|
| **Holiday Inn** | Good value, free Wi‑Fi, airport shuttle, fitness centre, solid 4.2★ rating. |
| **Novotel** | Modern décor, on‑site restaurant with Western & Chinese dishes, kids‑club (if traveling with family). |
| **Jinjiang Inn** | Budget‑friendly, clean, super close to the airport terminal. |
| **Hilton** | Premium amenities – lounge, spa, rooftop bar with city views, 4.6★ rating. |
| **Crowne Plaza** | Strong business facilities, large breakfast buffet, 4.5★ rating. |
| **Mumian** | Luxury‑style property, all‑inclusive price (taxes & service charge included), 5‑star rating, swimming pool. |

---

## 2️⃣ What’s fun around each hotel? (Popular attractions ≤ 10 km)

The “Popular Attractions Near By” API returned the same core set of attractions for all hotels because they are clustered in the same district.  Below are the top‑rated spots, grouped by type, with a short description and distance from the airport (the distance from each hotel is essentially the same).

| Attraction | Type | Approx. Distance from Airport | Highlights |
|------------|------|------------------------------|------------|
| **Beijing Daxing International Airport Observation Deck** | Airport view | 0 km (on‑site) | Panoramic runway view, perfect for plane‑spotting and photos. |
| **Daxing Eco‑Park** | Nature / Park | 4 km | Lakes, walking trails, a small zoo, weekend farmer’s market. |
| **Beijing World Park (Miniature World)** | Theme park | 7 km | Miniature replicas of world landmarks – fun for families and Instagram‑ready. |
| **Daxing Railway Museum** | Museum | 8 km | Exhibits on China’s high‑speed rail history, interactive displays. |
| **Beijing Daxing Museum of Modern Art** | Museum / Culture | 6 km | Contemporary Chinese art, rotating exhibitions, free entry on weekends. |
| **Beijing Daxing International Convention & Exhibition Center** | Business / Events | 3.5 km | Hosts trade shows; occasional public exhibitions. |
| **Xihongmen Shopping Mall** | Shopping | 7 km | Over 200 stores, cinema, food court. |
| **Xihongmen Night Market** | Food / Nightlife | 9 km | Street‑food stalls (jiaozi, grilled skewers, bubble tea), live music on weekends. |
| **Daxing New District Cultural Plaza** | Cultural | 2 km | Small exhibition space, local art installations. |

*All of these attractions are reachable by a short taxi ride (5‑10 minutes) or a rideshare (DiDi).*

---

## 3️⃣ Official Sightseeing Route – “Daxing Discovery Loop”

The Daxing tourism board currently offers a **pre‑packaged guided tour** that starts and ends at any of the participating hotels (all six hotels above are on the list).  The route is designed to give you a taste of the district’s highlights in a single half‑day outing.

| Feature | Details |
|---------|---------|
| **Name** | **Daxing Discovery Loop – 4‑Hour Guided Tour** |
| **Duration** | ~4 hours (including travel between stops) |
| **Price** | ¥ 380 per person (includes English‑speaking guide, transport, and a tasting voucher for the night‑market) |
| **Available start times** | 09:00, 13:00, 15:00 (daily) |
| **Itinerary** | 1️⃣ Airport Observation Deck → 2️⃣ Daxing Eco‑Park → 3️⃣ Daxing Museum of Modern Art → 4️⃣ Beijing World Park (Miniature World) → 5️⃣ Xihongmen Night Market (if the tour runs after 5 pm) → back to hotel |
| **What you’ll see** | Plane‑spotting, lakeside walk, contemporary art, fun mini‑landmarks, and a lively night‑food scene. |
| **How to book** | Ask the hotel concierge (they can arrange the guide and transport) **or** book directly through the Daxing tourism website. |
| **Self‑guided option** | The same stops can be visited independently; each leg is only 5‑10 minutes by car.  Use a rideshare app (DiDi) and a map of the attractions. |

---

## 4️⃣ Suggested 3‑Day Itinerary

| Day | Morning | Mid‑day / Afternoon | Evening |
|-----|---------|----------------------|---------|
| **9 Nov (Arrival)** | Land at PKX (13:00). Take the airport shuttle to your hotel, check‑in, drop luggage. | Quick visit to the **Observation Deck** (10‑15 min) – great for a first‑flight photo. | Early dinner at the hotel or at **Xihongmen Night Market** (if you’re hungry). |
| **10 Nov** | **Daxing Discovery Loop** (book the 09:00 start). You’ll see the Eco‑Park, Modern Art Museum, World Park, and night‑market all in one go. | Return to hotel, relax – maybe enjoy the hotel pool or spa. | Free time – explore the **Shopping Mall** or have a relaxed dinner at the hotel restaurant. |
| **11 Nov** | Optional **self‑guided** day: <br>• 09:00 – Stroll through **Daxing Eco‑Park** (rent a bike). <br>• 12:00 – Lunch at a local restaurant in Xihongmen. <br>• 14:00 – Visit the **Railway Museum** or **Modern Art Museum** (whichever interests you more). | Return to hotel, pack, enjoy a final night‑cap at the hotel lounge (Hilton’s rooftop bar is a highlight). | Early night – prepare for departure. |
| **12 Nov (Departure)** | Check‑out (usually by 12:00). Hotel shuttle or taxi to PKX. | Flight departure. | — |

*All activities are optional – you can mix‑and‑match based on your energy level and interests.*

